{"slug":"permutation-in-string","title":"Does a Permutation Appear?","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"medium","order":145,"tags":["strings","sliding-window","anagram"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A fixed-size window of letter counts","body":["A block of `s` is a permutation of `p` exactly when it has the same length as `p` and the same letter counts. So slide a window of length `len(p)` over `s` and compare the counts of the window with the counts of `p`.",{"code":"need = counts of p\nhave = counts of s[0:m]\nif have == need: ...\nfor i in range(m, len(s)):\n    have[s[i]] += 1\n    have[s[i - m]] -= 1     # the window moved one place\n    if have == need: ..."},"Moving the window changes two counters only. Comparing two tables of 26 numbers costs a constant, so the whole scan is O(26 * n)."]},"statement":["You are given two words `p` and `s`. Print `yes` if some block of consecutive letters of `s` is a rearrangement (permutation) of `p`, otherwise print `no`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `p`.","The second line has `s`."],"outputFormat":["Print `yes` or `no`."],"constraints":["1 <= length of p, s <= 20000","Both words contain lowercase letters."],"examples":[{"input":"ab\neidbaooo\n","output":"yes\n","note":"The block ba is a permutation of ab."},{"input":"ab\neidboaoo\n","output":"no\n","note":"No block of length 2 has the letters a and b."}],"hints":["The block must have exactly `len(p)` letters.","Count the letters of `p` and of the current window.","When the window moves, add the new letter and remove the old one, then compare the two tables."],"starter":{"python":"p = input().strip()\ns = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String p = sc.next();\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["A fixed window of the length of `p` slides over `s`. Two table updates per step keep the window counts current, and equal tables mean a permutation."],"complexity":"Time O(26 * n), space O(1).","code":{"python":"p = input().strip()\ns = input().strip()\n\nm = len(p)\nfound = False\nif m <= len(s):\n    need = [0] * 26\n    have = [0] * 26\n    for ch in p:\n        need[ord(ch) - ord(\"a\")] += 1\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        have[ord(s[i]) - ord(\"a\")] += 1\n        if i >= m:\n            have[ord(s[i - m]) - ord(\"a\")] -= 1\n        if i >= m - 1 and have == need:\n            found = True\n            break\nprint(\"yes\" if found else \"no\")\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int m = p.size();\n    bool found = false;\n    if (m <= (int) s.size()) {\n        vector<int> need(26, 0), have(26, 0);\n        for (char ch : p) need[ch - 'a']++;\n        for (int i = 0; i < (int) s.size(); i++) {\n            have[s[i] - 'a']++;\n            if (i >= m) have[s[i - m] - 'a']--;\n            if (i >= m - 1 && have == need) {\n                found = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << (found ? \"yes\" : \"no\") << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String p = sc.next();\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        int m = p.length();\n        boolean found = false;\n        if (m <= s.length()) {\n            int[] need = new int[26];\n            int[] have = new int[26];\n            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) need[p.charAt(i) - 'a']++;\n            for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n                have[s.charAt(i) - 'a']++;\n                if (i >= m) have[s.charAt(i - m) - 'a']--;\n                if (i >= m - 1 && Arrays.equals(have, need)) {\n                    found = true;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(found ? \"yes\" : \"no\");\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"ab\neidbaooo\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"ab\neidboaoo\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"ab\na\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"abc\ncba\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"bcbaabcbaabcaabacbbabaabbbbaccaccbbacbaabaaabbbcba\\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"bcbaabcbaabcaabacbbabaabbbbaccaccbbacbaabaaabbbcba\\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"bcbaabcbaabcaabacbbabaabbbbaccaccbbacbaabaaabbbcba\\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"yes\n"}]}